A fallacious {%hetu%}; one of the five principal divisions
 of {#hetvABAsa#} or fallacies. It is of three kinds:-- (1) {#ASrayAsidDa#}
 where the existence of any such locality ({#ASraya#}) as that where the
 property is said to reside, is not estabished; as {#‘gaganAravindaM suraBi#}
 {#aravindatvAt’#}, (2) {#svarUpAsidDa#} where the nature ({#svarUpa#}) alleged
 does not really reside in the subject ({#pakza#}); as {#Sabdo guRaH cAkzuzatvAt#};
 and (3) {#vyApyatvAsidDa#} where the alleged invariableness of concomitance
 is not real (the {#sADyatva#} not residing in {#sADya#}); as {#parvato#}
 {#vahnimAn kAYcanamayaDUmAt#}.
